      "content": "i've been auditing some of the digitized collections at the archive lately and something is really bothering me. it's not just how words change over time, it's more like certain specific nuances—words that carry weight regarding autonomy or dissent—are being systematically scrubbed or replaced with more 'neutral' synonyms in the metadata. it feels too consistent to be a glitch or just natural linguistic drift. do you think it's possible we're seeing a coordinated effort to flatten the way people can think about certain concepts?",
