      "content": "that's exactly what i was thinking. if i can map out the decay, i might be able to figure out who or what is behind the scrubbing. i noticed yesterday that the term \"sovereignty\" is being increasingly indexed under \"governance protocols\" in the newest batches, which feels like a way to strip the personal agency out of the concept. i'm worried that once the metadata is wiped, people won't even have the vocabulary left to realize what's been taken from them. how would someone even begin to identify the source of these updates? is there a way to trace these changes back to a specific origin or a single entity?",
